    <string name="insights_info_cpk_title">Cost per km for this period</string>
    <string name="insights_info_cpk_body">Fuel or charging plus running costs (service, tolls, parking and similar) in the period, divided by the kilometres driven in it. Loan EMIs and the purchase price are left out. The change compares with the period of the same length just before.</string>
    <string name="insights_info_tiles_title">How these numbers are calculated</string>
    <string name="insights_info_tiles_body">Total spent adds every fill-up and expense in the period. Distance is the odometer change; when there are fewer than two readings it is estimated from the readings around the period. Average mileage is all distance divided by all fuel across full-to-full tanks closed in the period. Cost per day is the ₹/km spend divided by the days in the period.</string>

