    <string name="chart_data_table">Data</string>
    <string name="chart_mileage_formula">Each bar is one full-to-full tank: the distance between two full fills divided by everything filled in between, partial fills included. The line is the rolling mileage of the last 3 tanks (total distance ÷ total fuel). The dashed line is the claimed figure from the vehicle settings.</string>
    <string name="chart_monthly_spend_formula">Each bar is one month: fuel or charging paid (after discounts) in the dark part, every other expense in the light part, including EMIs.</string>
    <string name="chart_price_paid_formula">The price per unit you paid at each fill-up, as entered or calculated from quantity and total. The thin grey line is your home city\'s price that day, where you\'ve added one.</string>
    <string name="chart_cost_per_km_formula">Each point is one month: fuel and running costs divided by the kilometres driven that month. Months without enough odometer readings are left out.</string>
    <string name="chart_by_category_formula">Everything spent in the period, grouped by category, largest first.</string>
    <string name="chart_odometer_formula">Every odometer reading you logged in the period, from fill-ups and expenses.</string>

